// The popped value is a parameter rather than the first operand of the same
// `+` chain that also reads the new length. `id` does not say what order the
// two sides of a `+` are evaluated in, and the two targets answer differently
// -- the C one inherits C's, the LLVM one is left to right -- so an expression
// that pops and measures at once prints a different length on each. That is
// docs/SPEC.md 10, S11, and this line is what found it.
pop_line(int v, int[] xs) {
  print("list: pop=" + v + " len=" + len(xs));
} return void;
